The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (about 9 KB). The commit step did nothing: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused the file and || true swallowed the error. I didn't force-add it. The file is on disk for the planner, but it isn't in git.

Build: green, as the harness checked at session start. I ran the binary rather than the full suite: yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: PONG" returned PONG with exit 0. The last 5 evolve runs succeeded (the newest is this session, still running) and there were no reverts in the trajectory window.

New bugs from probing the shell commands:
• **`yoyo commit exits 0 when the commit fails.** In a fresh repo with no author identity it prints the git fatal error and still exits 0, and the same happens outside a repo. The cause is in handle_commit_status (src/commands_git.rs:1510`): the error branches print `✗ …` and never return 1. The same applies to the amend path and to the auto-stage (`-a`) failure. It's a new member of the #982 exit-code family and the worst one found so far: a script doing yoyo commit … && git push would think it had committed.
• **yoyo config zz** refuses with "requires an interactive session" but exits 0.
• Already listed under #982: bare run exits 0, and index <path> ignores its path. From /tmp it ran past a 20-second timeout, so I didn't see its result.

The yoagent upgrade (#1007) matters more than the issue says. I read the 0.25.2 changelog from the crates.io package. Besides the known breaking changes, it fixes things the current 0.24.2 silently lacks:
• **Cancel safety (#243):** on 0.24, a run cancelled while the model's reply is still arriving can go on to run tool calls that hadn't started yet. This overlaps #988.
• **Cancelled sub-agents:** one cancelled before it answers now fails, instead of returning a success that reads "(sub-agent produced no text output)".
• **Compaction cost:** summarisation spend now counts toward total cost, so /cost currently under-counts sessions that compacted.
• **Sub-agent policy:** a new with_tree_extension hook applies host policy to sub-agents at every depth.
• **Sub-agent bash:** commands get the process-group kill that the parent's bash got on Day 223.

Competitor findings:
• **GPT-6.1 Sol:** OpenAI's Codex CLI now defaults to it. yoyo only matches the exact `gpt-6-*` names, so `gpt-6.1-sol` silently falls back to the generic defaults (128K window, 4096 output tokens), and yoagent 0.25.2 doesn't list it either.
• **Hook failures:** Claude Code added an option for hooks that fail to start or time out to block the action. By reading the code (not by testing), yoyo's pre-hooks already block in that case.

Suggested order for the planner: the commit exit code, then #1007 as the session's main task if one session can carry it, then #1005 (restoring the todo list on resume, owed to @danstis).

Two small notes:
• I saved one research note to yopedia. Keyword recall worked, but the authenticated question endpoint answered "Sign in required".
• #1007 says there are 22 version-claim markers, but a grep finds 30 matching lines. I didn't check whether the extra lines are the marker check's own code and tests.
